Cell["\<\
The existing name retains its global-monodromy meaning: transport around \
every closed base walk must be the identity.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"820c2c99-3887-42c1-981f-b20b4b05c612"],

Cell["\<\
Equivalently, the projection is injective on every connected component of the \
connection graph.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"8b36109d-e03b-47cd-ab4a-e9d6394b543d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The test includes every disconnected base component and first requires ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraConnectionQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraConnectionQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "10ef647a-0cbf-46a3-ad3e-88235bb2e4c9"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"16a8c9b2-9d77-4ebf-8b10-a806b4f19ad6"],

Cell["\<\
A graph supplies no faces, so this predicate is not a curvature test relative \
to a face system.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"bcb815b0-87d2-4644-bc9f-d45ce270ab3f"],

Cell["\<\
Every complete connection over a forest has trivial monodromy.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0ef3ea2c-3ebf-4fba-914b-453cb0a8623f"],

Cell["\<\
An empty collection returns False. The unique empty connection on a base \
without edges has trivial monodromy.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b7c609ac-6c69-43a8-aef9-ddaeb6904372"]
}, Open  ]],

